        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "f96d5a39-5965-58ca-806c-a486efbcf60a",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Plants: Colocasia, Coronilla, Xanthosoma\n- Plant Families: Araceae\n- Places: southeastern Asia, Indian subcontinent, Europe, North Africa\n- Topics: flowering plants, ornamental plants, horticultural names\n\nFacts:\n- Colocasia is a genus of flowering plants in the family Araceae that is native to southeastern Asia and the Indian subcontinent.\n- Coronilla is a genus containing about 20 species of flowering plants native to Europe and North Africa.\n- Many species of Xanthosoma, especially Xanthosoma roseum, are used as ornamental plants.\n- In popular horticultural literature, Xanthosoma species are called ape or elephant ear because their leaves are said to resemble an elephant's ear.\n- The common name elephant ear is also sometimes applied to similar plants in the closely related genera Caladium, Colocasia, and Alocasia.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
